From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Micha=C5=82=20Kope=C4=87?= <michal.kopec@3mdeb.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:05:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] slaunch: txt: take the Linux MLE size from the MLE header on
 EFI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On an EFI launch GRUB reports the MLE size of a Linux kernel as the PE
SizeOfImage less the setup sectors, which also covers .bss and the
image's padding. The kernel's MLE header ends the MLE at _edata. The
SINIT ACM of an Emerald Rapids platform (BIOS SINIT 20231116) rejects
the launch with "Reported MLE size doesn't correspond to values in
header" when GRUB reports 0x1338000.

Take the size from the MLE header for Linux on Intel TXT as well, as is
already done for other EFI images. The MLE page tables still map the
whole image. Linux uses the MLE size only to check that the event log
and the AP wake block do not overlap the MLE, and GRUB places both
below the page tables.

The AMD Linux launch keeps measuring the whole image, since the SKL and
the PSP DRTM service hash the DLME range GRUB reports and that range has
been tested on hardware.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Michał Kopeć <michal.kopec@3mdeb.com>
---
 grub-core/loader/slaunch/x86_efi_linux.c | 19 +++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/grub-core/loader/slaunch/x86_efi_linux.c b/grub-core/loader/slaunch/x86_efi_linux.c
index 54a37860d..dfdbda718 100644
--- a/grub-core/loader/slaunch/x86_efi_linux.c
+++ b/grub-core/loader/slaunch/x86_efi_linux.c
@@ -155,16 +155,15 @@ sl_efi_load_mle_data (struct grub_slaunch_params *slparams,
   slparams->mle_header_offset = mle_hdr_offset;
   slparams->mle_entry = mle_hdr->entry_point;
 
-  if (!is_linux)
-    {
-      /*
-       * The current value of the field covers the whole EFI image which can
-       * include a lot of useless padding.  Limit the size used for measuring
-       * MLE to that reported by the header.  Don't change the behaviour for
-       * Linux in case it causes trouble (needs testing).
-       */
-      slparams->mle_size = mle_hdr->mle_end - mle_hdr->mle_start;
-    }
+  /*
+   * The current value of the field covers the whole EFI image which can
+   * include a lot of useless padding.  Limit the size used for measuring
+   * MLE to that reported by the header.  The SINIT ACM rejects an MLE size
+   * that does not correspond to the header, so this applies to Linux on
+   * Intel TXT too.  The AMD Linux launch keeps measuring the whole image.
+   */
+  if (!is_linux || slparams->platform_type == SLP_INTEL_TXT)
+    slparams->mle_size = mle_hdr->mle_end - mle_hdr->mle_start;
 
   return GRUB_ERR_NONE;
 }
